Maintainer: João V. B. Dornelas <joaovitordornelas@hotmail.com>
Description: Provides an automated, reproducible, and scalable workflow for
    integrative plant taxonomy by combining herbarium specimen records,
    morphological data, ecogeographic information, and multivariate analyses.
    The package retrieves specimen records from major online biodiversity
    repositories, including GBIF, Jabot, Reflora Virtual Herbarium, and
    speciesLink, and integrates them into a standardized dataset. It provides
    tools for data cleaning and validation, construction of customizable
    morphological trait matrices, and analysis of morphological and
    ecogeographic variation using methods such as principal component analysis
    (PCA), k-means clustering, and non-metric multidimensional scaling (NMDS).
    The workflow supports reproducible species delimitation by producing
    standardized analytical outputs, including figures, tables, maps, and
    diagnostic summaries.
